From: Yehor Hrabovskyi <55855551+Egoushka@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:52:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Collapse people by name with one grouped pass
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GET /Persons lists one row per lowercased name, keeping the lowest id.
The correlated NOT EXISTS compared every row with every other row,
because lower(Name) cannot use the Name index, so the cost grew with the
square of the Peoples table. A GROUP BY lower(Name) with MIN(Id) picks the
same rows in one pass.

Adds tests for the case-only collapse, the kept id and paging.

